## Analysis direction
When the binder REJECTs the Application lane of a count-2 attempt, the attempt's Completion lane stays half-open on the connector and in the binder's incomplete
pair (joined by RID). The connector's intent then starts the next attempt whose Completion lane arrives while the old one is still registered → duplicate lane →
READY protocol error for the set (spec-conformant symptom of a connector that did not tear down its whole lane set first). Owner: the connector-side lane-set
lifecycle (session/pair generation) — a lane failure or rejection must close both lanes of that generation and only then re-open with the next generation
(one rule, spec line ~253). Check also the binder side: an incomplete pair whose Application lane was rejected/terminated must not keep accepting sibling
lanes (the pair is dead once any lane of it terminates). Do not add a retry/delay or accept duplicate lanes.

